<title>SWEDEN: Adtranz says wins one bln Skr Norway order.</title>
<headline>Adtranz says wins one bln Skr Norway order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adtranz Sweden and Adtranz Norway, units of ABB Daimler-Benz Transportation, said on Wednesday they won an order for fast trains from Norway's railway company Norske Statsbaner NSB worth around one billion crowns.  </p>
<p>The order involves 16 four-wagon trains with an option for another five train sets, the company said, adding that the order is conditional on approval from NSB's board.</p>
<p>The order is based on an option for a previous order of 16 three-wagon trains to the Gardermoen airport railway just outside Oslo which is under construction.</p>
<p>The trains will be in use from 1999.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
